{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["The days of Yisrael drew near to death — wherever a person wishes to command his sons, it must say ויקרבו. And likewise: ״ויהי כי זקן יצחק וגו׳״, ״ויקרא את עשו וגו׳״, ״לא ידעתי יום מותי״. And likewise: ״ויקרבו ימי דוד למות ויצו את שלמה בנו״. And the real beginning of this pericope is from ״וישב ישראל בארץ מצרים וגו׳״, for upon it ״ויחי יעקב״ is contiguous, except that the congregations did not wish to close the pericope of VaYigash at ״בותהי הארץ לפרעה״ [i.e., הארץ לפרעה], so they closed it at וישב ישראל." "Please place your hand — I have already explained it in connection with Avraham's servant."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {0 "The reading בותהי הארץ appears corrupt; rendered hyper-literally as it stands. The intended reference is to Genesis 47:20, כי את כל אדמת מצרים לפרעה, the actual end of the VaYigash narrative."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:30.957822267Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}